# Ansible Vault Password File Example
#
# This file should contain your vault password on a single line.
# 
# Setup Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .vault_pass.example .vault_pass
# 2. Edit .vault_pass and replace this content with your actual vault password
# 3. Secure the file: chmod 600 .vault_pass
# 4. NEVER commit .vault_pass to version control!
#
# The .vault_pass file is used to decrypt ansible/group_vars/all/vault.yml
# which contains sensitive credentials for:
#   - Hetzner Robot API
#   - Hetzner S3 Object Storage
#   - GitHub Actions SSH key
#
# For more information, see docs/vault-setup.md
